    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d106">

                <pb facs="0183" n="115" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v01/pg115"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72111/1073½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the
                            Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-30">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 30, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Lansing</hi>: As I intimated to you, I
                    gave the matter very serious thought when the question of the submarines was
                    brought up. I feel that it is really our duty (in the <hi rendition="#underline"
                        >spirit</hi>, at any rate, of the <hi rendition="#italic">Alabama</hi>
                    decision) to prevent submarines being shipped from this country even in parts,
                    and I hope that you will find a way of checking and preventing this if it is
                    contemplated.</p>
                <p>Always</p>
                <p>Cordially and faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodrow Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
